00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:15.615
seven years after launching to space

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:16.850
and NASA's spacecraft

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:19.019
delivered a capsule containing the sample

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:20.253
early on Sunday morning.

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:21.654
And we are told that that capsule

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:22.922
contains dust

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.624
and rocks from the asteroid.

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:25.992
Scientists will now spend years

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:28.161
studying the rare cosmic gift,

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:29.029
hoping to understand

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:30.630
the details about the origins

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:31.664
of the solar system.

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:31.998
With us

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:33.400
at the table, astrophysicist

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.802
Jan 11, Celso, professor of physics

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:36.603
and astronomy

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:37.504
at Barnard College

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:38.772
of Columbia University

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:40.106
and the author of the book

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:41.574
Black Hole Survival Guide.

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:42.675
